 r←Test_Log_105(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;msg;rc;L;lines
⍝ `ProcessLogFile` tells whether the last log entry is from the month of the given timestamp, and
⍝ with that whether it needs calling again before the month changes: housekeeping relies on it
⍝ in order not to read the whole log file every few seconds.
⍝ The log holds data from January to March 2024.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetTempDir'-Log/'
 rc←'Create!'F.CheckPath tempDir
 Assert rc
 L←##.Server.Logs
 lines←⊃F.NGET(∆TEMP_TEST_DATA,'/LogFile/app-log.txt')1
 lines←('2024-'∘≡¨5↑¨lines)/lines
 (⊂lines)F.NPUT(tempDir,L.GetLogFilename)1

 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≢L.ProcessLogFile tempDir(2024 3 4)    ⍝ The last entry is from March: done for March
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≢L.ProcessLogFile tempDir(2024 4 1)    ⍝ April has begun but nothing was logged in it yet

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
